hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  answering a question from one of my  LinkedIn group members so LinkedIn is  helping knew that I'm getting more and  more involved in and this is part of a  b2b what's a good b2b social media  market I think something like that and  so Janice wrote in with a question to  say I'd like to learn the quickest way  to learn about social media for business  I've been working in communications at a  software company for more than 14 years  I haven't had to use social media  because the company's market is very  specialized and when required however  I'm currently looking for another job in  communications and while I have a strong  writing editing background in both  English and French I've never done web  2.0 it seems to be a strong requirement  from any communications jobs I see how  do I fill this gap quickly so great  question Janice thanks for it it is  definitely a skill set that is in demand  and that if you're looking for a job in  communications you're going to have to  know and the more you can position  yourself as an expert the better in  terms of getting started I do actually  have a worksheet to help entrepreneurs  with their with their social media  skills but I don't want to turn this  into a sales page you can check that out  if you want to stop my site but my main  strategies for getting started with  social media is first to monitor so if  you can't use it for your company right  now I would try to look at ways to use  it for yourself  so I'd either look for ways to use it  for your technology company or look for  ways to use it yourself a brain yourself  as an expert and I would first start by  monitoring so monitoring is basically  looking for anybody who mentions your  name your company name your website and  phase one is just recognizing champions  so this is how I got started into social  media my first Avenue was through  Twitter and I thought Twitter was was  really stupid like people are talking  about their cats with you for lunch why  is this relevant to me I did a search my  company name the website and I found  that people were talking about my  business and I wasn't a part of the  conversation and you want to be wherever  your customers are right so phase one is  just recognizing your champions and  saying thank you you know everything was  good fortunately all the stuff that was  about my web  that being talked about was all good  awesome but you always want to make sure  that you're involved with your customers  and you're hanging out where they are so  that's that's kind of step one just  monitoring key terms and thanking people  or responding to criticism if you do get  any that are out there the next step is  I try to look for ways to get involved  in the conversations that are happening  and try to position yourself as an  expert so if you're now trying to get a  job in a new field especially in  communications it would help for them to  see that you really know what you're  talking about on social media and so you  could become or start becoming a social  media thought leader and you can share  your experiences with how you're  learning about it you can ask people  questions who are more advanced in the  field so to build a rolodex of contacts  you can potentially interview people who  are really good at it and share their  secrets or interview people who are in  the roles that you want to be at or  we're having a success at social media  at bigger companies that maybe that's  where you eventually you want to get to  you'll not only learn from them but  you'll you'll build an expertise set  yourself people will look forward to  seeing the content that you're creating  here and you're building a contact list  of people who you can lie on if you have  questions down the line eventually you  want to move from being the one asking  all the questions to being the one also  giving advice and you can either do it  from people asking you questions you may  not have any now so you know all these  videos that I do are coming from  questions from my audience so I don't  have to kind of make up questions that  come in to me but if you don't have an  audience yet at the beginning you can  participate in forums or you can look at  other tweets that are happening or other  LinkedIn discussion groups and instead  of answering the question in that forum  you can create a video or you can create  a blog post or you can create a LinkedIn  post and then make it detailed show how  you're an expert you're you know what  you're talking about  and link to it so people can then  comment on it so it can be really scary  if you've never done it before just like  any new thing and it can often be  overwhelming and for you know for you  get trying to get into that field it is  a new skill set that you should ideally  pick up again I'd start off really  simple basic put in words relating to  your current company and related to  yourself and just monitor at the start  and then slowly start to get involved in  discussions share what you think might  work but also ask questions and  interview people who are experts in the  field so you have unique content that  you can share and if you're part of this  b2b social media marketing group that  we're both members of you can learn a  lot from that group where you can also  for people who you who you meet and  connect with there you can do an  interview with them you can learn from  their success and you can post that  content up on the LinkedIn group and  then as people read it they'll come to  associate your name with these awesome  interviews and expert thought leadership  around social media one of my favorite  examples of this is a guy named Michael  Dunlop he's a young entrepreneur in the  UK he started a blog called income diary  that I don't think he's a part of  anymore or maybe his brothers writing or  something like that but the start of it  was really good where he was a young  entrepreneur who basically didn't know  anything about setting up an online  business and so he went out and  interviewed some of the most successful  people people who became his mentors and  guides about how to run an online  business and the first blog posts were  basically just him asking questions and  eventually he became known as a guy to  go to for how to run an online business  and he gained  expert status even though he wasn't  sharing the information himself he was  pulling it from these other people who  he respected and so in the process he  learned a lot about how to how to be an  expert in that field he made a lot of  great contacts and mentors who he can go  to on going for repeat information  repeat help and then he was eventually  the brand himself as that expert so  people would come to him as he learned  through the process so it's a great way  to get started to learn quickly by  talking to people who've already done  what you're trying to do and shortcut  your way to success  and that's that's kind of how I  recommend you getting started and I'm  excited to hear about your progress and  hopefully you're posted either on  YouTube or in our LinkedIn group so  thank you for the questions those you  watching if you like the video please  give a thumbs up below makes you want to  do more for you and if you have a  comment about this video or question  about you  own business or challenge you're facing  feel free leave in the comment section  below I always read those I love seem to  come in and I look forward to be able to  answer them for you so thank you and  I'll see you on the next episode  you
 

